Package: 1bit-kernel-image-@KVER@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: 1bit <packages@1bit.gg>
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Depends: 1bit-kernel-modules-@KVER@ (= @VERSION@), initramfs-tools, kmod
Provides: linux-image
Description: 1bit OS: our kernel for the appliance
 Linux @KVER@ as this appliance runs it: amdgpu (the GPU and
 /dev/kfd), amdxdna (the NPU), the board's EC and NPU support, built
 and signed with the enrolled MOK, so shim under Secure Boot hands
 over to it. The initramfs is generated by this package's postinst
 from initramfs-tools, as on any Ubuntu box; the modules are in
 1bit-kernel-modules-@KVER@. The previous kernel version stays
 installed on an upgrade, which is what makes the rollback work.
